    {
      "title": "Prospectus Summary",
      "excerpt": "PROSPECTUS SUMMARY 1 THE OFFERING 8 SUMMARY CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL DATA 10 RISK FACTORS 11 CAUTIONARY NOTE REGARDING FORWARD-LOOKING STATEMENTS 26 USE OF PROCEEDS 28 DIVIDEND POLICY 29 CAPITALIZATION 30 DILUTION 31 MANAGEMENT\u2019S DISCUSSION AND ANALYSIS OF FINANCIAL CONDITION AND  RESULTS OF OPERATIONS 32 BUSINESS 41 MANAGEMENT 49 COMPENSATION OF OUR EXECUTIVE OFFICERS 54 CERTAIN RELATIONSHIPS AND RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS 56 PRINCIPAL STOCKHOLDERS 59 DESCRIPTION OF CAPITAL STOCK 60 SHARES ELIGIBLE FOR FUTURE SALE 64 UNDERWRITING 66 MATERIAL U.S.\u00a0FEDERAL INCOME TAX CONSEQUENCES TO NON-U.S.\u00a0HOLDERS 71 LEGAL MATTERS 73 EXPERTS 73 WHERE YOU CAN FIND MORE INFORMATION 74 INDEX TO THE CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS F-1 This prospectus is not an offer to sell and does not constitute a solicitation of an offer to buy any of the shares offered hereby in any jurisdiction where the offer or sale ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Use of Proceeds",
      "excerpt": "Use of proceeds We expect to receive net proceeds from this offering of approximately $18,150,000, or approximately $20,925,000 if the underwriter exercises its over -allotment option in full, at the assumed public offering price of $6 per common share, after deducting estimated underwriting discounts and commissions and non -accountable expense allowance, as well as estimated other offering expenses payable by us, totaling approximately $1,850,000, or $2,075,000, respectively. We intend to use the net proceeds from this offering primarily to fund our acquisition strategy, including the acquisition of smaller, regional fabricators, and to a lesser extent for investments in technology, upgrading fabrication equipment, geographic expansion, and general corporate purposes. See \u201cUse of Proceeds.\u201d Dividend policy We do not anticipate paying any cash dividends on our common stock in the forese",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Risk Factors",
      "excerpt": "Risk factors Investing in our Class\u00a0A common stock involves a high degree of risk. See \u201cRisk Factors\u201d beginning on page\u00a011 of this prospectus for a discussion of factors you should carefully consider before deciding to invest in our common stock. The number of shares of our Class\u00a0A common stock to be outstanding after this offering is based on 5,141,250 shares of our common stock outstanding as of September 30, 2026 and excludes other shares of our Common Stock reserved for issuance under our 2026 Incentive Award Plan. Unless otherwise indicated, this prospectus reflects and assumes the following: \u2022 no exercise by the representatives of the underwriters of their over -allotment option; and \u2022 no exercise of the representatives\u2019 warrants. 9 Table of Contents SUMMARY CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL DATA The following tables set forth our summary consolidated financial and other data as of the dates ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dilution",
      "excerpt": "DILUTION If you invest in our Class\u00a0A common stock (the \u201cCommon Stock\u201d), your ownership interest will be immediately diluted to the extent of the difference between the public offering price per share and the pro forma net tangible book value per share of our Common Stock after this offering. Net tangible book value per share represents our total tangible assets less total liabilities, divided by the number of shares of our Common Stock outstanding. As of June 30, 2026, our net tangible book value was $139,266, or $0.03 per share of Common Stock, based on 5,141,250 shares of common stock outstanding as of September 30, 2026. For purposes of the per share calculations in this section, we have given effect to the Corporate Conversion completed on August 20, 2026, pursuant to which the membership interests of Onyx Capital Tequila Partners IV LLC were converted into shares of Common Stock of",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Principal Stockholders",
      "excerpt": "PRINCIPAL STOCKHOLDERS The following table sets forth the beneficial ownership of our common stock as of September 30, 2026, by: \u2022 each person, or group of affiliated persons, whom we know to beneficially own more than 5% of our common stock; \u2022 each of our named executive officers; \u2022 each of our executive officers; \u2022 each of our directors; and \u2022 all of our executive officers and directors as a group. The percentage ownership information shown in the column labeled \u201cPercentage of Shares Outstanding\u201d is based upon an aggregate of 6,691,250 shares of Common Stock and Series A Preferred Stock issued and outstanding as of September 30, 2026, consisting of 5,141,250 shares of Common Stock and 1,550,000 shares of Series A Preferred Stock. In computing the number of shares of Common Stock beneficially owned by a person and the percentage ownership of such person, we deemed to be outstanding all ",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Dividend Policy",
      "excerpt": "Dividend policy We do not anticipate paying any cash dividends on our common stock in the foreseeable future. See \u201cDividend Policy.\u201d Voting rights Each holder of our Class\u00a0A common stock is entitled to one vote per share. Each holder of our Series A preferred stock is entitled to 100 votes per share. Holders of our Class\u00a0A common stock and Series A preferred stock will vote together as a single class on all matters, except as required by law or our Certificate of Incorporation. NYSE American and NYSE Texas symbol We intend to apply to list our Class\u00a0A common stock on the NYSE American and the NYSE Texas under the symbol \u201cKATX.\u201d 8 Table of Contents Lock-Up In connection with this offering, our directors and officers and certain holders of our Class\u00a0A common stock as of the effective date of this registration statement will enter into customary \u201clock -up \u201d agreements in favor of the underw",
      "status": "source_excerpt_not_model_conclusion"
    }
  ],
